<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Ossetia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetia">Ossetia</a> is a region on the southern slopes of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, inhabited largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ossetians">Ossetians</a>. Clashes there marked the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in 1918–1920; it became an autonomous oblast in Soviet Georgia, broke away after the war of 1991–1992, and after the 2008 Russo-Georgian War was recognised as independent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-ossetia.jpg" alt="South Ossetia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Various · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Ossetia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
